<article class="env-definition" id="01CV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01CV">Definition <span data-tag="01CV">17.25.7</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Given an invertible sheaf $\mathcal{L}$ on $X$ we define the <em>associated graded ring</em> to be </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Gamma _*(X, \mathcal{L}) = \bigoplus \nolimits _{n \geq 0} \Gamma (X, \mathcal{L}^{\otimes n})  \]
</div>
  <p> Given a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules $\mathcal{F}$ we set </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Gamma _*(X, \mathcal{L}, \mathcal{F}) = \bigoplus \nolimits _{n \in \mathbf{Z}} \Gamma (X, \mathcal{F} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{L}^{\otimes n})  \]
</div>
  <p> which we think of as a graded $\Gamma _*(X, \mathcal{L})$-module. </p>
</article>